  "interpretation": {
    "vs_trained_baselines": "Ours (Signal-Check, training-free) has much higher embedding fidelity than both trained baselines: +13.84 dB vs Robust-Wide (95% CI [13.59, 14.09], paired n=600) and +5.62 dB vs TrustMark (95% CI [5.46, 5.78]); win rate 100.0% and 99.7% of images respectively.",
    "vs_training_free_dwt_dct": "Against the training-free DWT-DCT baseline the difference is -0.98 dB (95% CI [-0.99, -0.98]) -- statistically distinguishable at n=600 but small (~0.98 dB, i.e. <2% in MSE terms); both sit far above the trained baselines. So the defensible claim is 'fidelity at parity with the classical training-free baseline and far above the trained baselines', not 'better than DWT-DCT'.",
    "caveat": "TrustMark attacked_ba has only n=228 (detection succeeded on 38% = 228/600 of attacked images), so its attacked BA is subject to survivor bias."
